tes.com/transition-and-variable-charge-metals/","line":372},{"title":"[1","target":"https://www.matrix.edu.au/the-beginners-guide-to-the-periodic-table/groups-3-12-transition-metals/","line":372},{"title":"image.png","target":"Ikatan Kimia/image 2.png","line":490,"embedded":true},{"title":"Two O's connected by a double line. There are two pairs of dots next to each O.","target":"https://cdn.kastatic.org/ka-content-images/15d383d4d729ce64266ca86e821779690d7d5e83.svg","line":500,"embedded":true},{"title":"Two red balls connected by two gray sticks","target":"https://cdn.kastatic.org/ka-content-images/3fa0d9e97477b099eef2be738b74a65e99562469.png","line":500,"embedded":true},{"title":"An O connected to two H's by single lines. There are two pairs of dots next to the O.","target":"https://cdn.kastatic.org/ka-content-images/23e5ede2f679ec1fd1cc6f0cfa26742bfab35345.svg","line":501,"embedded":true},{"title":"A red ball connected to two white balls, each by one gray stick. The molecule has a V shape.","target":"https://cdn.kastatic.org/ka-content-images/3ad8e20821d90fe50e8025716d03db8280e5502e.png","line":501,"embedded":true},{"title":"A black ball is connected to two red balls, one on each side. Each red ball is connected to the black ball by two gray sticks. The molecule has a straight shape.","target":"https://cdn.kastatic.org/ka-content-images/92dae54dd949f1ba3e85aabbc0fa8944273d0ad5.png","line":502,"embedded":true},{"title":"A C connected to two O's, each by a double line. There are two pairs of dots next to each O.","target":"https://cdn.kastatic.org/ka-content-images/f3fc67d66b6eccc658636ee84d8950b2b35f25de.svg","line":502,"embedded":true},{"title":"A C connected to four H's, each by a single line.","target":"https://cdn.kastatic.org/ka-content-images/84acf1f96e1242284f96b6871fd15cb04aad5ecc.svg","line":503,"embedded":true},{"title":"A black ball is connected to four white balls, each by one gray stick. The white balls stick out in different directions, forming a 3D tetrahedral shape.","target":"https://cdn.kastatic.org/ka-content-images/d7f507ef384d269ae85837d5c28032464367690b.png","line":503,"embedded":true},{"title":"An N connected to three H's, each by a single line. There is a pair of dots next to the N.","target":"https://cdn.kastatic.org/ka-content-images/1ccf13821dbc87f50f01519c17c378be17f81817.svg","line":504,"embedded":true},{"title":"A blue ball is connected to three white balls, each by one gray stick. The white balls are all slightly below the blue ball in different directions, forming the shape of a shallow mountain.","target":"https://cdn.kastatic.org/ka-content-images/7bd7000f74a71aebd1c9b47e6e1dae511b9c9f7a.png","line":504,"embedded":true},{"title":"Many red and gray balls connected in a net-like pattern. Each connection consists of a single gray stick.","target":"https://cdn.kastatic.org/ka-content-images/23eebebf32ef3490b087dff5b366993588b8c093.png","line":522,"embedded":true},{"title":"A cube-shaped lattice consisting of smaller purple balls and larger green balls arranged in an alternating pattern.","target":"https://cdn.kastatic.org/ka-content-images/3f903df61d7027558f5c480436c19fdd8e72c3f9.png","line":540,"embedded":true}],"task_lines":[],"tasks":{},"codeblock_ranges":[]},"smart_blocks:Wiki of My Life/Persiapan Belajar Kelas XI/Kimia/Ikatan Kimia.md#Ikatan Kimia": {"path":null,"last_embed":{"hash":null},"embeddings":{},"text":null,"length":0,"last_read":{"hash":"120lz65","at":1785671881167},"key":"Wiki of My Life/Persiapan Belajar Kelas XI/Kimia/Ikatan Kimia.md#Ikatan Kimia","lines":[1,13],"size":699,"outlinks":[{"title":"A periodic table showing the common charges of ions formed by elements in different groups. Group 1, the first column, has a column charge of 1+. Group 2 has a common charge of 2+. Group 13 = 3+. Group 14 = 4+ or 4-. Group 15 = 3-. Group 16 = 2-. Group 17 = 1-. Elements in groups 3 through 12 form multiple charges.","target":"https://cdn.kastatic.org/ka-perseus-images/2ed38cf1808ecb46389e